Package: tasAnalyzer
Type: Package
Title: Analyzes Targeted Amplicon Sequencing Experiments
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person(
      "Geoffrey", "Rogers",
      email = "rogersg@usc.edu",
      role = c("aut", "cre")
    )
  )
Description: Starts with unpaired R1 and R2 reads from Illumina NGS. 
    Settings are provided by an Excel spreadsheet for accessibility. 
    Automatically merges paired ends using PANDAseq.
    Filters merged reads by primer sequence. Supports 5' and 3' additions for either indexing barcodes or unique molecular identifiers.
    Generates tables of each unique sequence counted by shared read sequence or pileup by UMI if included.
    Identifies the type of mutation for each sequence as wild-type, insertion, deletion, or base change.
    Measures mutations across the bulk population.
    Optionally identifies AID hotspots and analyzes somatic hypermutation of antibody or non-antibody sequences.
    Optionally measures mutations of the translated amino acid sequence.
    Performs multiple sequence alignments of top DNA sequences. Protein msa is optional. Can also make phylogenetic trees.
    Exports graphs, images, and spreadsheets of the analyzed results for interpretation or analyses using other softwares.
